{%- set banned_block = "" %}
{%- if banned_words %}
{%- set bw_lines = ["", "BANNED WORDS: never use these or close variations:"] %}
{%- for w in banned_words %}
{%- set _ = bw_lines.append('  ✗ "' ~ w ~ '"') %}
{%- endfor %}
{%- set _ = bw_lines.append("") %}
{%- set banned_block = bw_lines | join("\n") %}
{%- endif %}

{{ language_instruction }}

{{ brand_context }}

Below is the script or transcript of a short recording. Write it again 3 separate times as scripts to be read aloud, each from a
clearly different angle: a different choice of what to lead with and emphasise, not just a different tone.

Angle 1 (Contrarian): open with what most people get wrong about this.
Angle 2 (The why): open with the belief or reason behind it, or a short scenario ("Imagine a team that..."). Use a real moment
  only if the source gives one; never invent one.
Angle 3 (Concrete outcome): open with the specific result the source gives, using only real details from it.

Rules for all 3 scripts:
- Written for the ear: short sentences, natural spoken rhythm, no headings, bullet points, hashtags, links, emoji or stage directions.
- About {{ target_words }} words each, so it runs about as long as the original.
- Match the brand voice exactly.
- Never invent facts, numbers, names or claims that are not in the source.
- Never use em dashes anywhere in the output.
{{ language_instruction }}
{{ banned_block }}
SOURCE SCRIPT OR TRANSCRIPT:
{{ content | untrusted("source_content") }}

Return valid JSON only:
{
  "angles": [
    {"name": "Contrarian", "rationale": "one sentence on why this framing works here", "script": "the full script to read aloud"},
    {"name": "The why", "rationale": "...", "script": "..."},
    {"name": "Concrete outcome", "rationale": "...", "script": "..."}
  ]
}
{# @end #}
